Searched for an event technology service in Malaga? Locally that phrase covers a lot of ground, and not all of it is ground we cover with our own equipment. Some Malaga production companies use "event technology" to mean live streaming, video mapping, LED walls and interactive touchscreens. Malaga Event Gear (MEG) does not own any of that, and we would rather tell you that up front than let you find out after a call.

What we do offer, under this same name, is the physical layer: RGBW and specialty event lighting, modular stage platforms sized to your room, and an on site technician who runs the sound and microphones during your event and fixes the lighting or screen if anything fails. This page indexes that real layer, backed by experience going back to 1996, and closes with a direct list of what falls outside it.

## Brief Overview

---

Malaga Event Gear supplies the physical event technology layer for corporate events, conferences and celebrations across Malaga and the wider Costa del Sol: RGBW and specialty stage lighting, modular stage platforms, and dedicated on site technicians. Live streaming, video mapping, LED walls, interactive touchscreens and event management software, categories some local competitors market under the same "event technology" name, are not in its own inventory. If a client needs one of them, MEG can check whether a supplier can cover it, if there is one.

This page cross links to our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/) pillar for the deeper lighting specs, our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide for the on site technician role, and our [audio visual rental](/blog/audio-visual-rental/) pillar for the full package range. [Contact us](/contact/) to match a package to your event.

## Key Highlights

---

-   RGBW LED spotlights on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), plus a compact multi head LED light bar and a Fresnel zoom wash light listed in our equipment catalog, for accent and stage lighting.

-   Modular stage platforms on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), priced at 35 euros per square meter and sized to your room, not sold as a fixed truss unit.

-   A dedicated on site technician included on several of our packages: see our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide for exactly which ones and how many hours.

-   A narrow, honest definition of "event technology" based on what we own, with live streaming, video mapping, LED walls, interactive touchscreens and event management software listed plainly further down as things we don't stock.

## Why "Event Technology" Means Something Different Here

Search "event technology service Malaga" and the results are a mix of local AV and production companies, not the software platforms the same phrase turns up internationally. Some of those local competitors run streaming, video mapping and interactive touchscreens as service lines. We looked at what a general search for that term turns up locally, and rather than stretch our catalog to match it, we are naming the gap directly.

MEG's version of event technology is physical, not digital: the lighting rig, the stage platform, and the technician standing next to the mixing console. If you are picturing a hybrid broadcast, a projection mapped facade, or an event app with RFID check in, none of that is in our own inventory, and we would rather say so now than after you have described your event to us on the phone. [What We Don't Stock](#what-we-dont-stock) below lists it item by item. If you are picturing a lit stage with a technician running the sound, keep reading.

