## Event Lighting

Three real products sit under event lighting technology. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) includes 2 light bars with RGBW LED spotlights, a color changing accent fixture you run yourself, published at 290 euros ex VAT for up to 50 guests. Our equipment catalog also lists a compact 4 head LED light bar with foot pedal control, a Fresnel zoom wash light for larger corporate stages, and a wireless battery powered uplighting kit of 6 fixtures, the kind of wash, accent and floor lighting you would want for a keynote stage or a gala dance floor rather than a small private party.

We do not publish a standalone package line or a fixed price for any of these three fixtures the way we do for the Eco Pack's light bars. [Contact us](/contact/) with your venue and guest count and we will confirm what is possible. For the full spec sheet on all three fixtures, including where they sit inside our wider catalog, see [RGBW Spotlights, Specialty Stage Lighting and Uplighting](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/#rgbw-spotlights-specialty-stage-lighting-and-uplighting) on our audiovisual equipment rental service pillar. We are not duplicating that detail here. For the uplighting kit specifically, honest coverage for 2 to 4 venue features and a comparison against these RGBW spotlights, see our [stage uplighting](/blog/stage-uplighting/) guide.

![Color wall wash lighting alongside sound equipment set up for a formal event in the province of Malaga.](https://cdn.malagaeventgear.com/blog/1272/malaga_sound_lighting_rental_event-scaled-700x523.webp)

Color wall wash lighting alongside our sound equipment, set up for a formal event in the province of Malaga.

## Stage Design and Setup

Stage design at MEG means one real, priced product: modular stage platforms on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), an optional add on at 35 euros per square meter, sized to your room rather than sold as a fixed unit. It is a platform to raise speakers, a panel or a small band above floor level, not a scenic build.

We deployed exactly this for a two day corporate project with [Bmotion in Marbella](/blog/news-malaga-event-gear-delivers-premium-technical-support-for-bmotions-high-profile-corporate-project-in-marbella/), where modular platforms created the elevated presentation area the client needed for international guests.

![Modular stage platforms set up for a corporate presentation in Marbella.](https://cdn.malagaeventgear.com/blog/3076/2026.05.19-20-Bmotion-Marbella-3-1024x576.webp)

The modular staging deployed for the Bmotion Marbella project, alongside the gooseneck and wireless microphone systems that ran from the same platform.

Truss, pipe and drape, backdrop hardware and scenic theatrical staging are not in our own inventory. Our own crew also does not rig or hang equipment overhead, so a truss rig or anything flown above a stage would be work for a specialized supplier. See [What We Don't Stock](#what-we-dont-stock) below for how we handle a request like that. For the fuller staging breakdown alongside our lighting and screen inventory, see [Modular Staging for Corporate Events](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/#modular-staging-for-corporate-events) on our audiovisual equipment rental service pillar.

## On Site Technical Support

A technician is part of several MEG packages, running the sound and microphones for the duration of your event, and fixing the screen or lighting if anything fails, rather than leaving you to operate a rack of gear yourselves. We are not re answering the coverage details here: our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide covers exactly which packages include a technician, how many hours each one covers, and what the role does and does not include on site.

## What We Don't Stock

A general search for event technology in Malaga turns up services from local production companies that are not part of our own inventory. Here is the honest list:

-   **Live streaming or hybrid event streaming.** Cameras, streaming encoders and a recording service are not part of our own equipment. You bring your own laptop, your conferencing software and your internet connection. Our [audio visual rental for virtual events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-virtual-events/) guide has more detail.

-   **Video mapping, LED walls or video walls.** Our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/) pillar is explicit: our large format display is a single 60 inch flat panel, not a modular tiled video wall, and our projector setups don't include facade projection or outdoor mapping.

-   **Interactive touchscreens or kiosks.** Not part of our own inventory. For what we do set up at a ceremony or service, see our [audio visual rental for religious events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-religious-events/) guide.

-   **Interpretation, translation equipment or audience response/voting systems.** We do not stock this equipment ourselves, but we arrange it through a subcontracted partner for corporate and congress grade events: [contact us](/contact/) with your requirements. See our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/#what-we-dont-stock) pillar for the same note.

-   **Event apps, RFID tracking or ticketing technology.** Not in our own inventory, and not something our own crew runs. The event technology competitors we researched for this page are physical AV and production companies too, not registration or ticketing platforms.

Interpretation and voting already run through a partner. For the rest of this list, and for the truss or scenic staging mentioned under [Stage Design and Setup](#stage-design-and-setup), describe what you have in mind and we can check whether a supplier can cover it, if there is one. Anything that has to hang overhead would be rigged by that specialized supplier, never by our own crew.

